  "adaptations": [
    "Restored the corresponding original TypeScript sources instead of maintaining compiled JavaScript.",
    "Applied project formatting and import sorting.",
    "Shared query length and search-mode constants; removed unused MCP-server exports.",
    "Retained readonly array types after Array.isArray checks.",
    "Removed equivalent duplicate case-insensitive character ranges and impossible zero-length wildcard branches.",
    "Resolve original MCP identities through the pinned DSH public-name mapping, and reject identifier fragments as exact callable references.",
    "Extracted into a standalone project; machine-specific source locations are omitted from the source candidate.",
    "Fixed review regressions by preserving provider-aware exact matching while excluding foreign identifiers, and validating admissible MCP server-name delimiter boundaries.",
    "Moved the maintained retrieval engine from vendor/core to src/core as product source; original module paths and hashes remain relative to the core root.",
    "Prioritize unambiguous positive registered-name references before BM25 truncation, including embedding-outage fallback; retain pattern and successful hybrid ranking.",
    "Expose the existing Ollama model-name validation pattern for shared settings validation; retain the pinned local endpoint and opt-out of remote embeddings.",
    "Added provider-neutral embedding operations, native OpenAI-compatible and Ollama clients, provider-scoped caches and an explicit local-only disabled mode.",
    "Propagate per-operation cancellation through native discovery, the retrieval controller and embedding HTTP requests; preserve independent callers and treat abort separately from provider failure."
  ],
